<% content_for :title, "Reflections | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="perspectives-reflections-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="perspectives-reflections-hero">

    <div class="perspectives-reflections-hero-content">

      <p class="perspectives-reflections-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / PERSPECTIVES / REFLECTIONS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>SHIT</span>
        <span>I'VE BEEN</span>
        <span>THINKING</span>
        <span>ABOUT.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="perspectives-reflections-intro">
        THINGS I'VE LEARNED.<br>
        THINGS I'VE QUESTIONED.<br>
        THINGS I HAVEN'T FUCKING FIGURED OUT YET.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="pr-section pr-section-black">

    <p class="pr-number">01 / REFLECTIONS</p>

    <h2>
      I DON'T HAVE<br>
      A FUCKING<br>
      THESIS.
    </h2>

    <div class="pr-copy">

      <p>
        These aren't answers.
      </p>

      <p>
        They're things I've been thinking about while getting sober,
        living with bipolar disorder, dealing with consequences,
        trying to understand myself, and figuring out what the hell
        I want my life to look like now.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some of these thoughts will probably change.
      </p>

      <p>
        Good.
      </p>

      <div class="pr-callout">
        I'M ALLOWED TO LEARN SOMETHING<br>
        AND CHANGE MY FUCKING MIND.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- REFLECTIONS -->
  <section class="pr-reflections">

    <div class="pr-reflections-heading">

      <p>02 / THINGS ON MY MIND</p>

      <h2>
        THINKING<br>
        OUT<br>
        LOUD.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Notes from wherever the fuck I am in the process.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="pr-grid">


      <!-- REFLECTION 01 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-pink">

        <p class="pr-card-number">01</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          RECOVERY
        </p>

        <h3>
          RECOVERY<br>
          ISN'T FUCKING<br>
          LINEAR.
        </h3>

        <p>
          Progress doesn't always look like moving forward in a
          straight line. Sometimes it's recognizing the same pattern
          a little earlier than I did last time.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            What if progress is measured by how differently I respond,
            not by never struggling again?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- REFLECTION 02 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-yellow">

        <p class="pr-card-number">02</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          IDENTITY
        </p>

        <h3>
          WHO THE FUCK<br>
          AM I WITHOUT<br>
          THE CHAOS?
        </h3>

        <p>
          When chaos has been part of life for long enough,
          stability can feel strangely unfamiliar.
        </p>

        <p>
          That doesn't necessarily mean something is missing.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            Which parts of me are actually me — and which parts
            were survival, addiction, illness, or habit?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- REFLECTION 03 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-purple">

        <p class="pr-card-number">03</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          CONSEQUENCES
        </p>

        <h3>
          TWO THINGS<br>
          CAN BE TRUE.
        </h3>

        <p>
          I can understand why I did something without pretending
          the thing I did was okay.
        </p>

        <p>
          Explanation and accountability aren't enemies.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            Can I take responsibility without turning responsibility
            into permanent self-hatred?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- REFLECTION 04 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-black">

        <p class="pr-card-number">04</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          BIPOLAR
        </p>

        <h3>
          I AM NOT<br>
          EVERY STATE<br>
          MY BRAIN ENTERS.
        </h3>

        <p>
          My brain can change dramatically.
          Mood can change. Energy can change.
          Thoughts can change. Perception can change.
        </p>

        <p>
          That raises a weird question about identity.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            What stays underneath all those changing states?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- REFLECTION 05 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-yellow">

        <p class="pr-card-number">05</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          ADDICTION
        </p>

        <h3>
          MAYBE THE<br>
          DRINK WASN'T<br>
          THE WHOLE STORY.
        </h3>

        <p>
          Alcohol was a problem.
        </p>

        <p>
          But removing alcohol doesn't automatically answer why
          escaping myself felt so fucking appealing in the first place.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            When I want out of my own head, what am I actually
            trying to get away from?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- REFLECTION 06 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-pink">

        <p class="pr-card-number">06</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          CONTROL
        </p>

        <h3>
          NOT EVERYTHING<br>
          IS MINE TO<br>
          FUCKING CONTROL.
        </h3>

        <p>
          Other people get to misunderstand me.
          They get to dislike me.
          They get to make decisions I wouldn't make.
        </p>

        <p>
          I still get to decide what I do next.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            How much energy am I wasting trying to control
            shit that was never mine?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- REFLECTION 07 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-purple">

        <p class="pr-card-number">07</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          SPIRITUALITY
        </p>

        <h3>
          "I DON'T KNOW"<br>
          IS STILL AN<br>
          ANSWER.
        </h3>

        <p>
          I don't need a perfect explanation for the universe,
          spirituality, consciousness, death, or whatever the hell
          is bigger than me.
        </p>

        <p>
          Mystery doesn't automatically need to be solved.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            What happens when I let myself wonder without demanding
            certainty?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- REFLECTION 08 -->
      <article class="pr-card pr-card-black">

        <p class="pr-card-number">08</p>

        <p class="pr-card-topic">
          STARTING OVER
        </p>

        <h3>
          STARTING OVER<br>
          IS STILL<br>
          STARTING.
        </h3>

        <p>
          Starting over can feel humiliating when I compare where
          I am to where I think I should already be.
        </p>

        <p>
          But standing still because I'm embarrassed about starting
          over doesn't get me anywhere either.
        </p>

        <div class="pr-card-question">
          <span>WHAT I'M ASKING</span>

          <p>
            What would I build if I stopped treating starting over
            like proof that I failed?
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>


    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CONTRADICTIONS -->
  <section class="pr-section pr-section-yellow">

    <p class="pr-number">03 / CONTRADICTIONS</p>

    <h2>
      BOTH CAN<br>
      BE FUCKING<br>
      TRUE.
    </h2>

    <div class="pr-copy">

      <p>
        I'm getting increasingly suspicious of ideas that require
        everything to fit neatly into one category.
      </p>

      <div class="pr-both-grid">

        <div>
          <span>I CAN BE</span>
          <strong>GRATEFUL</strong>
          <p>and still be pissed off.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>I CAN TAKE</span>
          <strong>RESPONSIBILITY</strong>
          <p>without hating myself.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>I CAN HAVE</span>
          <strong>COMPASSION</strong>
          <p>and still have boundaries.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>I CAN BE</span>
          <strong>STRUGGLING</strong>
          <p>and still be making progress.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>I CAN</span>
          <strong>FORGIVE</strong>
          <p>without inviting somebody back in.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>I CAN</span>
          <strong>CHANGE</strong>
          <p>without pretending the past didn't happen.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- QUESTIONS -->
  <section class="pr-section pr-section-purple">

    <p class="pr-number">04 / QUESTIONS</p>

    <h2>
      SHIT I DON'T<br>
      KNOW THE<br>
      ANSWER TO.
    </h2>

    <div class="pr-copy">

      <p>
        I used to think reflection meant eventually arriving
        at an answer.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm less convinced now.
      </p>

      <div class="pr-questions">

        <p>Who am I when I'm not reacting?</p>

        <p>What am I still trying to prove?</p>

        <p>What does enough actually look like?</p>

        <p>What am I holding onto because it's familiar?</p>

        <p>Which stories about myself are outdated?</p>

        <p>What do I want when nobody else is watching?</p>

        <p>What am I afraid will happen if life gets quiet?</p>

        <p>What would I do differently if shame wasn't making the decision?</p>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CHANGING YOUR MIND -->
  <section class="pr-section pr-section-pink">

    <p class="pr-number">05 / CHANGING MY MIND</p>

    <h2>
      OLD ME<br>
      DOESN'T GET<br>
      A VETO.
    </h2>

    <div class="pr-copy">

      <p>
        I have believed things that I don't believe anymore.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've defended choices I wouldn't make now.
        I've misunderstood people.
        I've misunderstood myself.
      </p>

      <p>
        That's uncomfortable.
      </p>

      <p>
        It's also kind of the fucking point of learning.
      </p>

      <div class="pr-callout">
        IF NEW INFORMATION CAN'T CHANGE<br>
        MY MIND, THEN I'M NOT REFLECTING.<br><br>
        I'M JUST DEFENDING.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- WRITING -->
  <section class="pr-section pr-section-black">

    <p class="pr-number">06 / WRITE IT DOWN</p>

    <h2>
      GET IT OUT<br>
      OF YOUR<br>
      FUCKING HEAD.
    </h2>

    <div class="pr-copy">

      <p>
        Thoughts are slippery when they stay in my head.
      </p>

      <p>
        I can rationalize something, rewrite it, exaggerate it,
        minimize it, and convince myself it makes perfect sense.
      </p>

      <p>
        Writing makes me look at what I actually think.
      </p>

      <div class="pr-thought">
        SOMETIMES MY THOUGHTS SOUND A LOT LESS CONVINCING
        ONCE THEY'RE SITTING ON A PIECE OF PAPER.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="pr-ending">

    <p>
      NOTICE IT.<br>
      QUESTION IT.<br>
      WRITE IT DOWN.
    </p>

    <h2>
      KEEP<br>
      FUCKING<br>
      THINKING.
    </h2>

    <p class="pr-ending-copy">
      I don't need to finish every thought.
      Some of them are allowed to stay questions.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO PERSPECTIVES",
        perspectives_path,
        class: "pr-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>